-- title:
--   Supersingular specialisations of the H₁ datum have no q-torsion
-- statement:
--   Throughout, write $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ for `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` and, for the local data below, write $B$ for the valuation subring `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` of $k_0$ and $\mathcal C$ for the $B$-subalgebra [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin ↥B ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L142) of $K$, i.e. `chartAlg ↥B ↥K {j}`.
--
--   *Global arithmetic data.* A prime $q$, a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$ (`hqM'`), and a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ (`hℓg12`) and $\ell_g \mid M'$ (`hℓgM'`). A valuation subring $A$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ with `hA : A.LiesOverPrime q`, that is, $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over `ResidueField A` which, by `hW`, consists exactly of the elements of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, the places $w$ satisfying the predicate `IsSupersingularPlace q M' (ResidueField A)`; here a place is a valuation subring of the function field, distinct from the whole field, containing the image of the base field and a principal ideal ring. A distinguished element $s$ of $W$. The inclusion `hle` of intermediate fields `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`, i.e. the $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-field generated by the coefficientwise image of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` inside `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` is contained in `xHFunctionFieldBar (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`.
--
--   *Constant reduction.* A datum $R_0$ of type `ConstantReduction A ↥(modularFunctionFieldBar M') (modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M')`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, a surjective ring homomorphism `R₀.residue` from it onto `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` with kernel the maximal ideal, a push-forward `R₀.placeMap` on places preserving degrees, compatibility of the residue map with the residue map of $A$ on constants, the criterion that a constant lies in `R₀.integers` if and only if it lies in $A$, and the remaining normalisation clauses (existence of scalings with non-zero residue, and compatibility of `placeMap` with order divisors), summarised here. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires, for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that this element lie in `R₀.integers` and that its residue, viewed as a Laurent series over `ResidueField A`, be the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   *The local base.* An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$ (`hπ`). The hypotheses on $B$: it is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), it is a Henselian local ring (`hhens`), and its residue field is algebraically closed (`hres`). The hypothesis `hκ` requires every $a \in A$ to be congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to the image of some $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   *Roots of unity and the level structure.* An element $\xi \in k_0$ which is a primitive $(q\ell_g)$-th root of unity (`hξ`), together with `hιξ`: some ring homomorphism $k_0 \to \mathbb C$ sends $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell_g))$. A subgroup $H_1$ of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ which, by `hH₁`, is the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) — the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ — with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$. An intermediate field $K$ of `LaurentSeries ↥k₀` over $k_0$ which, by `hK`, equals [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange ↥k₀ (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), together with a $B$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with the tower $B \subseteq k_0 \subseteq K$. An element $j \in K$ whose image in `LaurentSeries ↥k₀` is the coefficientwise embedding of the $j$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) (`hj`), with $j \neq 0$.
--
--   *Functoriality hypotheses for the level components.* For every $B$-algebra $T$, every Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$ and every variable change $C$: `hℓ` states that [`ModularCurve.IsGamma1Point W ℓg D`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassGamma1Pow.html#L10) is carried to `IsGamma1Point (C • W) ℓg (D.variableChange C)` for every level datum $D$; `hM` states that `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` is carried to `IsGamma0PowAt (C • W) p k (ModularCurve.kernelVariableChangeDeg C (ModularCurve.gamma0PowDeg p k) h)`; `hL` states that if $h$ divides [`ModularCurve.inLineMulPoly W ℓg n x`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassH1Pow.html#L18) then `kernelVariableChangeDeg C d h` divides `inLineMulPoly (C • W) ℓg n (u^{-2}(x - C.r))`.
--
--   *Group laws and transport.* A family of relative group laws $\mathcal G$ over $B$ (`GroupLaws ↥B`) which is chord–tangent (`h𝒢`: each group law admits a points evaluation) and has the origin as identity (`h𝒢O`: each admits an origin-chart section with the two affine coordinates vanishing). A level transport $\mathcal T$ of type `LevelTransport ↥B 𝒢 q`, functorial in coefficient maps and equivariant for variable changes while preserving the level condition, satisfying `h𝒯 : 𝒯.IsSectionTransport`: the transported sections agree with the original ones after the identifications `Proj.map φ hφ` for graded homomorphisms realising variable changes, respectively coefficient changes. The hypotheses `hVC` and `hCO` supply, for each projective Weierstrass curve over a $B$-algebra and each variable change, respectively each $B$-algebra map, a graded ring homomorphism between the projective-model graded rings satisfying `IsVariableChangeHom`, respectively `IsCoefficientHom`, and carrying the irrelevant ideal appropriately.
--
--   *The moduli package.* Let $D$ denote the level moduli datum `(WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.rigidDataH1Pow ↥B ℓg M' q hℓ hM hL 𝒢 𝒯).toLevelModuliDatum`; its points over a $B$-algebra $T$ are classes of raw data (a Weierstrass curve over $T$ with unit discriminant together with level data satisfying the level condition) modulo variable change, and `jOf` is the $j$-invariant. A package $P_0$ of type `LevelModuliPackageAbs ↥B D` consists of a $B$-algebra `P₀.B₀`, a universal point `P₀.univ` over it, and the representability clause that every point over a $B$-algebra $T$ is `D.map φ P₀.univ` for a unique $B$-algebra map $\varphi$. Further, a point $x_0$ of $D$ over $K$ whose $j$-invariant, read in `LaurentSeries ↥k₀`, is [`ModularCurve.jqNModC ↥k₀ q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18), that is `qExpand ↥k₀ q (jqModC ↥k₀)` (`hx₀`), and a $B$-algebra map `clC` from `P₀.B₀` to $\mathcal C$ which, by `hclC`, becomes the classifying map `P₀.classify x₀` after composing with the inclusion $\mathcal C \subseteq K$.
--
--   *Conclusion.* For every ideal $y$ of $\mathcal C$ that is maximal, and every $B$-algebra homomorphism $\psi : \mathcal C \to$ `ResidueField ↥B` whose vanishing locus is exactly $y$ (that is, $\psi(c) = 0$ if and only if $c \in y$), the following implication holds.
--
--   Suppose that $y$ computes values at $s$, in the following sense: for every Laurent series $g$ over $\mathbb Q$ lying in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose coefficientwise image lies in `R₀.integers`, such that (i) for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, non-negativity of $P.\mathrm{ord}$ at the coefficientwise image of `jq` implies non-negativity of $P.\mathrm{ord}$ at the coefficientwise image of $g$, and (ii) the residue `R₀.residue` of that element lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, and such that the coefficientwise image of $g$ in `LaurentSeries ↥k₀` lies in $K$ and, as an element of $K$, lies in $\mathcal C$, one has: for every $c \in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$ and whose residue in `ResidueField A` equals the value at $s$, in the sense of `Place.evalAt`, of `R₀.residue` of the image of $g$, the difference between the element of $\mathcal C$ determined by $g$ and the image of $c$ under `algebraMap ↥B 𝒞` lies in $y$.
--
--   Then for every raw datum $x$ of `rigidDataH1Pow ↥B ℓg M' q hℓ hM hL 𝒢 𝒯` over `ResidueField ↥B` whose class `Quot.mk _ x` in the points of the datum over `ResidueField ↥B` equals `D.map (ψ.comp clC) P₀.univ`, every point $P$ of the affine curve `x.curve.toAffine` with $q \cdot P = 0$ is $0$.
--
--   Thus the specialisation of the universal point at the closed point $y$ carries a Weierstrass curve over the residue field of $B$ with no non-zero $q$-torsion point rational over that field.
--
--   This is the supersingularity input, in the shape needed for the $\Gamma_0(M') \cap \Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ moduli datum with auxiliary $q$-level: over a closed point of the integral chart at which the $j$-invariant specialises to a supersingular value, the reduced curve has no non-trivial $q$-torsion rational over the (algebraically closed) residue field. It is used by the statements producing a place with the required moduli behaviour at the Tate point, and by the identification of the associated moduli point, for the Drinfeld-level model of the modular curve of level $H_1$.
